Title: LOW TIDE
Credit: Written by
Author: Test Writer
Draft date: 10/12/26

INT. HARBOR OFFICE - NIGHT #1#

Rain on the glass. ANNA VOSS (40s) reads a file under a desk lamp.

THE PHONE RINGS.

ANNA
Voss.

MR. DELL (V.O.)
They found the boat. Pier nine.

ANNA
(standing)
Who found it?

MR. DELL (V.O.)
Kids. Don't come alone.

ANNA
NO.

CUT TO:

EXT. PIER NINE - CONTINUOUS #2#

Wind. A rusted trawler knocks against the pilings. COP #2 holds a flashlight.

COP #2
Detective. You're gonna want to see this.

ANNA
What is it? Tell me now, because I have been up since four and I am not walking onto that boat without knowing what I am walking onto.

COP #2
(beat)
It's Mrs. O'Neil's boy.

MRS. O'NEIL (O.S.)
Where is he?

Anna turns. MRS. O'NEIL, 60s, in a nightgown and boots, at the end of the pier.

ANNA
Ma'am, stay there.

INT./EXT. ANNA'S CAR - MOVING - LATER #3#

Anna drives. The wipers can't keep up.

ANNA
(into phone)
Dell. It's the O'Neil kid. Call his mother's priest.

MR. DELL (V.O.)
I'll call him.

> FADE OUT.
